# Benchmark: 3D render
# Workload: 3D vertex transformations, Euler angle rotations (X, Y, Z),
# perspective projection, surface normal rotation, backface culling,
# and Lambertian diffuse lighting over 15 frames of a 3D solid cube.
# Measures trigonometry (sine, cosine), custom object access, arithmetic,
# and condition evaluation.

a Vertex has
    x
    y
    z

a Face has
    nx
    ny
    nz

neg is 0 minus 1
pos is 1

vertices are empty
v0 is a Vertex with x neg, y neg, z neg
add v0 to vertices
v1 is a Vertex with x pos, y neg, z neg
add v1 to vertices
v2 is a Vertex with x pos, y pos, z neg
add v2 to vertices
v3 is a Vertex with x neg, y pos, z neg
add v3 to vertices
v4 is a Vertex with x neg, y neg, z pos
add v4 to vertices
v5 is a Vertex with x pos, y neg, z pos
add v5 to vertices
v6 is a Vertex with x pos, y pos, z pos
add v6 to vertices
v7 is a Vertex with x neg, y pos, z pos
add v7 to vertices

faces are empty
f0 is a Face with nx 0, ny 0, nz neg
add f0 to faces
f1 is a Face with nx 0, ny 0, nz pos
add f1 to faces
f2 is a Face with nx 0, ny pos, nz 0
add f2 to faces
f3 is a Face with nx 0, ny neg, nz 0
add f3 to faces
f4 is a Face with nx pos, ny 0, nz 0
add f4 to faces
f5 is a Face with nx neg, ny 0, nz 0
add f5 to faces

frames is 15
totalScreenX is 0
totalScreenY is 0
visibleFaces is 0
totalShading is 0

count from 1 to frames as frame
    rotX is frame times 6
    rotY is frame times 9
    rotZ is frame times 4

    sinX is sine of rotX
    cosX is cosine of rotX
    sinY is sine of rotY
    cosY is cosine of rotY
    sinZ is sine of rotZ
    cosZ is cosine of rotZ

    for each vertex in vertices
        vx is x of vertex
        vy is y of vertex
        vz is z of vertex

        y1_a is vy times cosX
        y1_b is vz times sinX
        y1 is y1_a minus y1_b

        z1_a is vy times sinX
        z1_b is vz times cosX
        z1 is z1_a plus z1_b

        x1 is vx

        x2_a is x1 times cosY
        x2_b is z1 times sinY
        x2 is x2_a plus x2_b

        z2_a is z1 times cosY
        z2_b is x1 times sinY
        z2 is z2_a minus z2_b

        y2 is y1

        x3_a is x2 times cosZ
        x3_b is y2 times sinZ
        x3 is x3_a minus x3_b

        y3_a is x2 times sinZ
        y3_b is y2 times cosZ
        y3 is y3_a plus y3_b

        z3 is z2

        depth is z3 plus 3.5
        px is x3 times 100
        projX is px divided by depth
        py is y3 times 100
        projY is py divided by depth

        screenX is round of projX
        screenY is round of projY

        totalScreenX is totalScreenX plus screenX
        totalScreenY is totalScreenY plus screenY
    .

    for each face in faces
        fnx is nx of face
        fny is ny of face
        fnz is nz of face

        ny1_a is fny times cosX
        ny1_b is fnz times sinX
        ny1 is ny1_a minus ny1_b

        nz1_a is fny times sinX
        nz1_b is fnz times cosX
        nz1 is nz1_a plus nz1_b

        nx1 is fnx

        nx2_a is nx1 times cosY
        nx2_b is nz1 times sinY
        nx2 is nx2_a plus nx2_b

        nz2_a is nz1 times cosY
        nz2_b is nx1 times sinY
        nz2 is nz2_a minus nz2_b

        ny2 is ny1

        nx3_a is nx2 times cosZ
        nx3_b is ny2 times sinZ
        nx3 is nx3_a minus nx3_b

        ny3_a is nx2 times sinZ
        ny3_b is ny2 times cosZ
        ny3 is ny3_a plus ny3_b

        nz3 is nz2

        ldot_x is nx3 times 0.577
        ldot_y is ny3 times 0.577
        ldot_z is nz3 times 0.577
        ldot is ldot_x plus ldot_y
        ldot is ldot plus ldot_z

        if ldot is less than 0
            ldot is 0
        .

        if nz3 is less than 0
            visibleFaces is visibleFaces plus 1
            scaledLight is ldot times 100
            lightIntensity is round of scaledLight
            totalShading is totalShading plus lightIntensity
        .
    .
.

say "3d render" frames "frames, screen coords" totalScreenX totalScreenY "visible faces" visibleFaces "shading" totalShading
